'''Nash Durango''' was a [[Gender|female]] [[human]] [[pilot]] and [[Technician|mechanic]] from the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] of [[Tenoo]] who lived during the [[High Republic Era]]. While she was still a child, Durango, along with her [[RJ unit]] [[droid]] [[RJ-83]], helped her [[Durangos|parents]]' [[Durango Shuttle Service|shuttle company]] and transported many things with her [[shuttle]], the ''[[Crimson Firehawk]]''.<ref name="The Young Jedi" /> She befriended the [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]], and [[Nubs]] and helped them during various adventures.<ref name="Meet the Young Jedi" />

==Biography==
===Family business===
Nash Durango was a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] who resided in [[Kublop Springs]] on the [[planet]] [[Tenoo]].<ref name="The Young Jedi" /> She was the daughter of [[Kryys Durango|Kryys]] and [[Ceeli Durango]],<ref name="Race Day" /><ref name="Feather Frenzy">{{YJA|Feather Frenzy}}</ref> who owned the shuttle company [[Durango Shuttle Service]].<ref name="THR Character Encyclopedia" /> While she was still a child, Durango, along with her [[RJ unit]] [[droid]] [[RJ-83]], helped her [[Durangos|parents]]' [[Durango Shuttle Service|shuttle company]] and transported many things with her [[shuttle]], the ''[[Crimson Firehawk]]''.<ref name="The Young Jedi" />

===New Jedi friends===
In [[232 BBY]], Durango was sent to [[Coruscant]] in one of the shuttles delivering [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi younglings]] to the [[Tenoo Jedi Temple|Jedi Temple]] on her [[homeworld]] Tenoo. While she waited for the Jedi younglings, she decided to repair the ''Crimson Firehawk''. Soon, three Jedi younglings [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]], and [[Nubs]] arrived as Durango finished the repair on the ''Crimson Firehawk''. They introduced themselves and then quickly got onboard to leave for Tenoo.<ref name="The Young Jedi" /> Along the way, they get some time to get to know each other.

[[File:Crimson_Firehawk_YJA_S1E1.png|thumb|300px|left|Nash was pilot of the ''Crimson Firehawk''.]]
When they arrived on Tenoo, Durango was contacted by [[Hap]], a [[chef]] who operated [[Hap's Sap Tap]] in Kublop Springs. He knew about her [[Jedi]] passengers and asked for help, as his [[Cafe|café]] was being [[Raid on Hap's Sap Tap|raided]] by a [[Taborr's gang|gang]] of [[pirate]]s led by [[Cyrus Vuundir|Taborr Val Dorn]]. They landed in Kublop Springs and Durango, who stayed with her ship, told the Jedi to [[Comlink|contact]] her if they needed help. After a fight between the [[Youngling|young]] Jedi and Taborr's gang, the pirates attempted to escape with their loot. The Jedi contacted Durango, who arrived with the ''Firehawk''. With RJ-83's help, she used a crane hook to pull up the cart with Hap's stolen belongings before the pirates could load it aboard [[Iron Talon|their starship]]. This distracted them long enough for the Jedi and several local residents to arrive, forcing the pirates to leave empty-handed. Durango later transported the Jedi to the temple.<ref name="The Young Jedi" /> And at the end of she gets invited to get a tour with Kai, Lys and Nubs on the Jedi Temple.

On another day Nash and her [[Jedi]] friends competed in a boat race against [[Raena Zess]] who always won the race because of how advanced her [[boat]] was. Both boats got stuck in some mud, so they had to work together to escape. Nash and the young Jedi eventually won the race and won a trophy from [[Hap]].<ref name="Race Day" /> 

==Personality and traits==
Nash Durango was a [[human]] [[Gender|girl]] with red hair, green eyes and fair skin.<ref name="THR Character Encyclopedia" /> She had two mothers named [[Kryys Durango|Krrys]] and [[Ceeli Durango]].<ref name="Race Day" /><ref name="Feather Frenzy" /> Durango was a confident pilot who learned how to fly [[starship]]s from her parents.<ref name="THR Character Encyclopedia" /> 

Durango was close to her droid co-pilot [[RJ-83]], whom she frequently carried. She and RJ were good friends with the [[Jedi Initiate]]s Kai Brightstar, Lys Solay and Nubs.<ref name="THR Character Encyclopedia" /> She is also respected [[Inaya]] due to her skills as a pilot and mechanic.

==Behind the scenes==
Nash Durango first appeared in "[[Meet the Young Jedi]]" the first short released before the premiere of the animated series ''[[Star Wars: Young Jedi Adventures]]''. Durango is voiced by [[Emma Berman]].<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|StarWars|status/1568748577681469440|[[Star Wars]]|quote=Incoming transmission. Jamaal Avery Jr. and Emma Berman star as Kai Brightstar and Nash Durango in Star Wars: Young Jedi Adventures coming in 2023.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/HmJEh}}</ref>

According to ''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]'', Nash Durango was set to appear in [[Star Wars: The High Republic|''The High Republic]] [[Phase III: Trials of the Jedi]], alongside [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]], and [[Nubs]].<ref name="THR Character Encyclopedia" /> Although the others did appear in Phase III,<ref name="The Finale">[[The High Republic – The Finale 1|''The High Republic – The Finale'' 1]]</ref> Nash did not.

